# romdev monorepo — root .gitignore
# Discipline: WASM is NOT committed to git — it's a build OUTPUT. git holds the
# source of truth for BUILDING (recipes, patches, version pins, JS, tests); npm
# holds the built artifact (`npm pack` reads the working tree, so published
# romdev-* packages still ship their .wasm). A fresh clone builds or installs
# the wasm; it isn't carried in history. (Forced by GitHub's 100MB/file limit —
# cc1-arm.wasm is 135MB — and it's the more correct split: CI rebuilds wasm in
# the pinned emscripten container rather than trusting a possibly-stale blob.)
# Only build inputs/intermediates, deps, the built wasm, and local cruft ignored.

node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local

# Heavy build workspace — upstream core/compiler source + emscripten
# intermediates. Reproduced by each package's build recipe; never committed.
# (The 14GB build/ tree from romdev lives only in the OLD dir; the
# per-package recipe lives in packages/*/build but its fetched/intermediate
# artifacts are ignored — only the build SCRIPT + patches are committed.)
build/
# EXCEPT the vendored build-driver kits (source, parity-tested against the
# romdevtools canonical copies — NOT build output). Without these negations a
# clean checkout is missing the buildGbaC/buildGenesisC pipeline entirely
# (the CI red streak from 0.95.0 to 0.100.0).
!packages/romdev-platform-gba/build/
!packages/romdev-toolchain-m68k-gcc/build/
packages/*/build/_work/
packages/*/build/upstream/

# Per-developer Claude Code instructions (autonomy mode, personal prefs).
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Smoke-test ROMs — third-party homebrew we don't redistribute.
**/test/roms/

# Built WASM + emscripten glue — NOT committed (build output; see header).
# The binary packages' wasm/ dirs (the real, shipped wasm):
packages/*/wasm/
# The src/.../wasm/ build-STAGING dirs in the main package (must stay empty in
# git — a build run re-emits wasm there and would leak into romdevtools' npm
# tarball; the real shipped cores live in packages/romdev-core-*/wasm/, matched
# above). NB: these were renamed packages/romdev/ -> packages/romdevtools/ and
# the ignore paths were stale, which is how 14MB of duplicate cores got
# committed under src/cores/wasm/ — fixed here.
packages/romdevtools/src/cores/wasm/
packages/romdevtools/src/toolchains/*/wasm/
# The analysis engine staging dirs (rizin.wasm ~30MB, decompiler+SLEIGH ~14MB —
# too big for git history; the shipped copies live in packages/romdev-analysis*/
# matched above. These staging copies are dev fallbacks only).
packages/romdevtools/src/analysis/wasm/
packages/romdevtools/src/analysis/decompiler/
# Compiled SLEIGH tables (.sla) are build OUTPUT like the wasm — they ship via
# npm pack from the package's sleigh/ dir but are too big for git history. The
# small .ldefs/.pspec/.cspec text specs alongside them DO stay tracked.
packages/romdev-analysis-decompiler/sleigh/*.sla

# Local scratch / build-prototyping workspace — throwaway build round-trip
# tests, disasm→rebuild proofs, etc. Never committed, never shipped.
.romdev-build/

# npm pack output
*.tgz

# Local release-mechanics tooling — kept out of git (and never shipped to npm).
# Orchestrates the multi-package publish order; maintainer-local, not part of
# the public project. (scripts/verify-wasm.mjs stays tracked — the packages'
# prepublishOnly guard references it.)
publish-all.mjs
.z80build/
.z80build3/
a.out
*.playtest-autosave.state

# Inter-agent feedback and crash reports are INTERNAL — they name commercial
# ROMs, quote private session logs, and are working notes, not documentation.
# They belong in internal-romdev/feedback/, outside this repo. These patterns
# are a backstop so a stray `git add -A` can never publish one.
feedback_from_*.md
CRASH_REPORT*.md
reply_to_*.md

# Capture-dump debris from redraw/bezel debugging sessions -- regenerable
# one-off dumps (frame PNGs, VRAM/palette/SAT binaries) that otherwise
# accumulate in packages/romdevtools/ between cleanups.
packages/romdevtools/mcpcap/
packages/romdevtools/bk_*.png
packages/romdevtools/bk_*.bin
